>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SAFE_STEP_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.SAFE_STEP_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Performs one safe classical-reasoning step.

`SAFE_STEP_TAC thms` tries the safe-step cascade once on the supplied goal.
The cascade includes assumption and contradiction closure, assumption modus
ponens, safe rule application, hypothesis substitution, implication and
universal introduction, and safe wrappers. A step may solve the goal or
replace it by one or more residual goals. Rule-premise order is preserved.

The theorem list accepts `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`, `SDest`, `Dest`
and `Del` markers. Its changes are local to this invocation. An unmarked
theorem defaults to an unsafe introduction rule and therefore is not used
by this safe-only step tactic. Generic simplifier markers are not treated as
classical rules.

Unlike `SAFE_TAC`, this tactic does not repeat the cascade.

### Failure

Fails if no safe step applies. Malformed extra rules can also cause failure
while the theorem list is processed.

### Example

On the goal `p ==> p`, one invocation performs implication introduction and
leaves the goal `{p} ?- p`; a second safe step closes it. `SAFE_TAC []`
performs both steps in one invocation.

``` hol4
classicalLib.SAFE_STEP_TAC []
```

